    "updated_at": "2026-01-22T07:48:16Z",
    "body": "See tests added in https://github.com/ExodusOSS/bytes/commit/7b2ca41c884cde37c63867cd940a8fb8b19387d2 and https://github.com/ExodusOSS/bytes/commit/8f308ba2b0a45afb050d9a8886a22736d219c2fe and comments about platforms there\n\nBoth commits are for cases of continuing a fatal stream after error\n\n---\n\nIn general, I think that continuing a fatal stream after error is deeply cursed, both here and in #358.\nContinuing does not work in Chrome on UTF-8 - errors get stuck in some cases\nNo setups should be using that and expect to work\n\nI wonder if the spec can just prohibit that instead of trying to figure out what to do with ISO-2022-JP and Unicode BOM states",
    "author_association": "NONE",
